    "description": "**Company Description**\nInfinity Quality Services (IQS) is a leading India-based provider of Inspection and Non-Destructive Examination (NDE) services, supporting diverse industrial sectors. The organization delivers a full range of inspection and training solutions, tailored to client requirements and conducted either on-site or at its dedicated training facilities. All inspections and training are performed by technicians and instructors certified to SNT-TC-1A requirements by the American Society for Non-Destructive Testing (ASNT), ensuring high technical standards. IQS offers hands-on expertise in Ultrasonic Flaw Detection, Ultrasonic Thickness Gauging, Magnetic Particle Inspection, Penetrant Testing, dimensional and hardness testing, and visual inspections. The company also specializes in inspections of static and rotary equipment, casting, forging, welding, automobile spares, plates, pipes, marine engine spares, and gears.\n  \n**Role Description**\nThe Graduate Engineering Trainee role is a full-time, on-site position based in Panihati. The trainee will support inspection and NDE activities by assisting senior engineers and technicians in preparing test setups, performing basic measurements, recording data, and documenting inspection results. Daily responsibilities include learning and applying relevant mechanical and manufacturing engineering principles, following established procedures and safety protocols, and helping in the execution of tests such as ultrasonic, magnetic particle, and visual inspections under supervision. The role involves collaborating with project teams, contributing to quality reports, and participating in continuous training to gain proficiency in inspection standards, equipment handling, and industry best practices. The trainee is expected to demonstrate initiative, maintain accurate records, and support timely completion of client projects.\n  \n**Qualifications**\n\n* Candidates should possess strong Mechanical Engineering and Manufacturing Engineering foundations.\n* Candidates should possess solid Analytical Skills and basic Project Management abilities.\n* Candidates should possess effective Communication skills for collaborating with teams and reporting findings.\n* Relevant internship or academic project experience in industrial, inspection, or quality-related environments is beneficial.\n* Bachelor\u2019s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related engineering discipline is preferred.\n* Ability to work on-site in Panihati, follow safety guidelines, and learn to operate inspection and NDE equipment.\n* Basic understanding of quality standards and an interest in developing expertise in NDE techniques and industrial inspections.",
