    "description": "Transport is at the core of modern society. Imagine using your expertise to shape sustainable transport and infrastructure solutions for the future. If you seek to make a difference on a global scale, working with next-gen technologies and the sharpest collaborative teams, then we could be a perfect match.\n  \n  \nWe value your data privacy and therefore do not accept applications via mail.\n  \n  \n**Who We Are And What We Believe In**\nWe are committed to shaping the future landscape of efficient, safe, and sustainable transport solutions. Fulfilling our mission creates countless career opportunities for talents across the group\u2019s leading brands and entities.\n  \n  \nApplying to this job offers you the opportunity to join\n**Volvo Group**\n. Every day, you will be working with some of the sharpest and most creative brains in our field to be able to leave our society in better shape for the next generation. We are passionate about what we do, and we thrive on teamwork. We are almost 100,000 people united around the world by a culture of care, inclusiveness, and empowerment.\n  \n  \n**Trucks Technology & Industrial Division**\nhire team players who are ready to create real customer impact. Our decentralized teams work close to our customers, with speed and autonomy, to build what they truly need.\n  \n  \nJoin us to collaborate on innovative, sustainable technologies that redefine how we design, build, and deliver value. Bring your curiosity, your expertise, and your collaborative energy, and together, we\u2019ll turn bold ideas into tangible solutions for our customers and contribute to a more sustainable tomorrow.\n  \n  \n**Graduate Apprentice Trainee \u2013 CAD/Creo (NATS)**\n**Location: Volvo Group India**\n**Program: National Apprenticeship Training Scheme (NATS)**\n**About Volvo Group**\nAt Volvo Group, we drive prosperity through transport and infrastructure solutions, shaping the future of sustainable mobility. As a global leader in the transportation industry, we are committed to developing innovative and sustainable engineering solutions.\n  \n  \nThrough the National Apprenticeship Training Scheme (NATS), we offer fresh engineering graduates an opportunity to gain practical industry experience, develop technical competencies and work alongside experienced professionals on real-world engineering projects.\n  \n  \n**Role Overview**\nAs Graduate Apprentice, you will support engineering design and development activities, gaining hands-on experience in Computer-Aided Design (CAD), 3D modelling, engineering drawings and product development processes. You will work with experienced engineering teams and learn to apply industry standards and engineering practices.\n  \n  \n**Eligibility Criteria**\n\n* Education: B.E. / B. Tech in Mechanical Engineering or Automobile Engineering.\n* Year of Graduation: 2024, 2025 or 2026.\n* Program Eligibility: Candidates must meet the eligibility requirements prescribed under the National Apprenticeship Training Scheme (NATS).\n* Experience: Fresh graduates; prior industry experience is not mandatory.\n* Academic Performance: Minimum 65% aggregate throughout academics (10th, 12th / Diploma and Graduation).\n\n**Key Skills & Technical Competencies**\n\n* Strong fundamentals in Mechanical / Automobile Engineering.\n* Basic knowledge of CAD software such as Creo, CATIA or SolidWorks.\n* Understanding of 2D engineering drawings, 3D modelling and design concepts.\n* Basic knowledge of engineering drawing standards, GD&T and manufacturing processes.\n* Proficiency in MS Office applications, particularly Excel, Word and PowerPoint.\n* Knowledge of Power BI, data analytics or programming will be an added advantage.\n* Good analytical, problem-solving and learning abilities.\n* Effective communication, collaboration and teamwork skills.\n\n**Program Duration**\nAs per the applicable National Apprenticeship Training Scheme (NATS) guidelines.\n  \n  \n**What You Will Gain**\n\n* Hands-on exposure to real-world automotive engineering and CAD design activities.\n* Opportunity to work with experienced engineering professionals.\n* Practical understanding of product development and engineering processes.\n* Development of technical, analytical and professional competencies.\n* Exposure to Volvo Group's engineering standards and global working practices.",
