    "description": "SNSIN | Full time\n  \n  \nTrainee - Network Security Engineer\n  \n  \nChennai, India | Posted on 24/09/2026\n  \n  \ncheck(event) ; career-website-detail => apply(record.id,meta)\" mousedown=\"lyte-button => check(event)\" final-style=\"background-color:#6875E2;border-color:#6875E2;color:white;\" final-class=\"lyte-button lyteBackgroundColorBtn lyteSuccess\" lyte-rendered=\"\"> check(event)\" mousedown=\"lyte-button => check(event)\" final-style=\"background-color: #fff; color:#FFFFFF;border-color:#FFFFFF;\" final-class=\"lyte-button lyteColorBtn\" lyte-rendered=\"\"> {{getI18n(\"zr.cw.sh.job\")}}\n  \n  \nShare this job with your network\n  \n  \n\n* openurl(event)\">\n* openurl(event)\">\n* openurl(event)\">\n* openurl(event)\">\n* openurl(event)\">\n* copyLink(event)\">\n* load\\_list\\_page(event)\"> Job listing\n* Job details\n\nJob Information\n  \n  \n\n* Date Opened 24/09/2026\n* Salary Trainee / fresher - 3.75 LPA\n* Job Type Full time\n* Industry IT Services\n* City Chennai\n* Province Tamil Nadu\n* Country India\n* Postal Code 600034\n\n**About Us**\nSNS India is a leading cybersecurity company specializing exclusively in information security solutions. With operations across 10+ locations in India, SNS delivers end-to-end cybersecurity services including consulting, implementation, training, and 24\u00d77 SOC support.\n  \n  \nPowered by 150+ cybersecurity experts, SNS serves 1,500+ clients with a strong 97% customer retention rate. Our offerings include security consulting, audit & compliance, vulnerability management, and identity & access management solutions.\n  \n  \nSNS is an ISO/IEC 27001 certified, Great Place to Work\u00ae (GPTW) certified, and CRISIL SME-1 rated organization, recognized with multiple awards across India and the APAC region.\n  \n  \nJoin SNS and build your career in one of the world\u2019s fastest-growing industries\u2014Cybersecurity.\n  \n  \nTo know more about us, visit us at: www.snsin.com\n  \n  \n**Job Description**\n\n* Assist in configuring and managing firewalls, VPNs, and other network security appliances.\n* Monitoring network engineering performance and ensure system availability and reliability.\n* Configuring and installing various network devices and services (e.g., routers, switches, firewalls, load balancers, VPN, QoS).\n* Performing network maintenance and system upgrades including service packs, patches, hot fixes and security configurations.\n* Monitor performance and ensure system availability and reliability.\n* Monitor system resource utilization, trending, and capacity planning.\n* Collaborate with senior engineers in troubleshooting and resolving network/security issues.\n* Stay updated on the latest security threats, trends, and technologies.\n\n**Requirements**\n\n* Bachelor\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.\n* Certifications: CCNA Mandatory, Fortinet NSE1-2 are a plus\n* Good understanding of basic networking concepts \u2013 TCP/IP, OSI Model, Routing & Switching.\n* Familiarity with firewalls, IDS/IPS, and endpoint security.\n* Basic knowledge of cybersecurity principles and practices.\n* Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n* Willingness to learn and adapt quickly in a fast-paced environment.\n* Good written and verbal communication skills.\n\ncheck(event) ; career-website-detail-template-2 => apply(record.id,meta)\" mousedown=\"lyte-button => check(event)\" final-style=\"background-color:#6875E2;border-color:#6875E2;color:white;\" final-class=\"lyte-button lyteBackgroundColorBtn lyteSuccess\" lyte-rendered=\"\">",
