    "description": "**Job Description Summary**\nEnsure an uninterrupted supply of materials to support production and sales. Work to resolve Materials issues while achieving and maintaining inventory business metrics.\n  \n  \nGE HealthCare is a leading global medical technology and digital solutions innovator. Our purpose is to create a world where healthcare has no limits. Unlock your ambition, turn ideas into world-changing realities, and join an organization where every voice makes a difference, and every difference builds a healthier world.\n  \n  \n**Job Description**\n**Roles and Responsibilities**\n\n* The Manufacturing / Materials Planner (also known as on site as a Production Controller) is responsible for generating a Master Production Schedule (MPS) to meet required output with available capacity and releases job cards in line with the plan.\n* The post holder will also manage shortages to maximize enablement and clear to build in order to drive on time starts and completes to MRP and collaborates closely with Flow Leaders/Production Line Managers to ensure buy-in and adherence to the plan.\n* Generate daily and weekly production schedule\n* Manage shortages to maximize clear to build and on time starts/finishes\n* Release job cards in line with MRP and action exception messages\n* Collaborate with ops team to provide output commits\n* Define daily/weekly production goals to track adherence to the plan\n* Collaborate with ops team to ensure resources are appropriately allocated and aligned to achieve the plan\n* The applicant must be a good team player flexible and be able to work to tight schedules.\n* Monitor the integrity of job card data to ensure MRP signals are correct\n\n**Required Qualifications**\n\n* Bachelor's degree in Mechanical /Electrical/Electronics/Biomedical Engineering\n* Recent graduate or up to 1 year of relevant internship or industrial experience.\n* Basic understanding of manufacturing processes and engineering fundamentals.\n* Good analytical and problem-solving skills.\n* Strong communication and teamwork skills.\n* Strong interpersonal and leadership skills\n* Strong problem solving skills\n\n**Desired Characteristics**\n\n* Internship or academic project experience in manufacturing, production engineering.\n* The successful candidate will be a motivated and enthusiastic individual\n* Eagerness to learn in a fast-paced manufacturing environment.\n* Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications for reporting and documentation.\n* Positive attitude with strong ownership and collaboration skills.\n\n**Inclusion and Diversity**\nGE HealthCare is an Equal Opportunity Employer where inclusion matters. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by law.\n  \n  \nWe expect all employees to live and breathe our behaviors: to act with humility and build trust; lead with transparency; deliver with focus, and drive ownership \u2013 always with unyielding integrity.\n  \n  \nOur\n**total rewards**\nare designed to unlock your ambition by giving you the boost and flexibility you need to turn your ideas into world-changing realities. Our salary and benefits are everything you\u2019d expect from an organization with global strength and scale, and you\u2019ll be surrounded by career opportunities in a culture that fosters care, collaboration, and support.\n  \n  \n**Disclaimer:**\n*GE HealthCare will never ask for payment to process documents, refer you to a third party to process applications or visas, or ask you to pay costs. Never send money to anyone suggesting they can provide employment with GE HealthCare.*\n******Additional Information******\n**Relocation Assistance Provided:**\nNo",
